{{!
    @template local_evidencehub/hub_choose

    The hub before a template is chosen: the heading with the template picker beside it, as the list and the matrix
    draw it, and one sentence asking for a template, or saying the context offers none.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * title - the page's heading.
    * picker - core's single select of the templates on offer, HTML.
    * locked, contextname - entered from a category: the page says it offers that category's templates only.
    * hastemplates - whether the context offers any template.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Evidence hub",
        "picker": "<form method=\"get\"><select name=\"templateid\"><option>Electricians</option></select></form>",
        "locked": true,
        "contextname": "Operations",
        "hastemplates": true
    }
}}
<div class="local-evidencehub-rview" data-region="local-evidencehub-choose">
    <div class="local-evidencehub-rview-pagehead">
        <h2 class="local-evidencehub-rview-title">{{title}}</h2>
        <div class="local-evidencehub-rview-picker">{{{picker}}}</div>
    </div>
    {{#locked}}
    <p class="local-evidencehub-rview-locked">{{#str}} hublocked, local_evidencehub, {{contextname}} {{/str}}</p>
    {{/locked}}
    {{#hastemplates}}
    <p class="text-muted">{{#str}} hubchoosetemplatefirst, local_evidencehub {{/str}}</p>
    {{/hastemplates}}
    {{^hastemplates}}
    <p class="text-muted">{{#str}} hubnotemplates, local_evidencehub {{/str}}</p>
    {{/hastemplates}}
</div>
